 "about_text": "Perrotin is an international contemporary art gallery founded in Paris in 1990 by Emmanuel Perrotin, then twenty-one years old. Over three decades the gallery has grown from a single Paris space into a network of more than twenty locations across Europe, Asia, and North America, including a gallery in Tokyo's Roppongi district. Perrotin's program is deliberately eclectic, spanning painting, sculpture, photography, and new media, and bringing together established figures, artists represented for decades, younger emerging talents, and several artist estates. The gallery describes its roster as spanning around eighteen nationalities and four continents, reflecting a stated commitment to diversity of generation, background, and medium rather than adherence to a single movement or aesthetic.",
